<article class="env-definition" id="059B">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/059B">Definition <span data-tag="059B">10.88.2</span>.</a> Let $f: M \to N$ and $g: M \to M'$ be maps of $R$-modules. Then we say $g$ <em>dominates</em> $f$ if for any $R$-module $Q$, we have $\mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(f \otimes _ R \text{id}_ Q) \subset \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(g \otimes _ R \text{id}_ Q)$. </p>
</article>